{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB12698 - MONDO_12268",
  "verbalization": "Ibalizumab is associated with Aids through a chain of indications that link it to HIV Infectious Disease, which in turn is linked to Aids. The evidence suggests that Ibalizumab may be repurposed for the treatment of HIV-related conditions, including Aids, through its role in treating HIV Infectious Disease. The shared indication of Hiv Infectious Disease across multiple paths indicates a potential overlap in therapeutic use, suggesting that Ibalizumab could be considered for repurposing in the context of Aids. The presence of multiple drugs (Elvitegravir, Zalcitabine, Doravirine) that are linked to Aids through the HIV Infectious Disease pathway supports the idea that Ibalizumab may have a role in treating HIV-related conditions, potentially offering a new therapeutic avenue for Aids. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering the broader context of HIV treatment in the repurposing of Ibalizumab.",
